        <obo1:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">The soybean or soya bean (Glycine max) is a species of legume native to East Asia, widely grown for its edible bean, which has numerous uses.  Traditional unfermented food uses of soybeans include soy milk, from  which tofu and tofu skin are made. Fermented soy foods include soy sauce, fermented bean paste, nattō, and tempeh.</obo1:IAO_0000115>
